## 7. Swap-ins by judge (about 15 seconds each, after the pitch)

- **NVIDIA.** [DEMO: Agents trace, one agent expanded.] "One live trajectory: Triage called `get_host_inventory`, found eleven co-resident guests, called `check_reachability`, saw the management port reachable, then wrote its finding with a blast score. Every row is tagged `model` or `fallback`, so you can see exactly what Nemotron did. Our logged live run: 15 turns, 14 tool calls, zero malformed."
- **Spacetime.** [DEMO: Policy view, then Screen B.] "The gate is the `propose_action` reducer. In one transaction it reads the policy row and the target and writes executed, pending or blocked; a refused action never commits, so it can't run. Reducers check the caller's identity: only an enrolled operator approves, only an admin adds people or changes policy. Both screens are just subscriptions."
- **Security / CISO.** [DEMO: Overview, click b14-gpu-07, Open secure shell.] "Click the host. Claura's CA mints a short-lived OpenSSH certificate for the read-only forensics principal; the host proves itself with a CA-signed host certificate, so there's no trust-on-first-use. Touch ID, then a second approver. Every session lands in a hash-chained ledger."
- **NMC².** [DEMO: War Room tasks, then the handoff card.] "Missed warning: six signals, one incident. Handoff: tasks with owners and Scribe's shift handoff on the same record, so the next shift doesn't rebuild the night from memory. The eleven neighbors restart on clean hosts; we never live-migrate them through a hypervisor we no longer trust."
- **Winstead attorney.** [DEMO: #legal, the decision log, the clocks card.] "Every decision carries a name and a timestamp. The notification clocks are examples labelled 'confirm with counsel', and they start only when counsel makes the call. The PDF is what you'd hand outside counsel the next morning."

