## 10. Why we win, track by track

**Winstead PC: Cyber Incident Response Dashboard.** We built to the brief and to the organizer's clarification (the attacker sees normal comms, phones are down, email is sporadic, nobody has information).

| Requirement | Claura, live |
|---|---|
| 1. Highly secure, isolated system inside a potentially compromised network | Command plane outside the network on SpacetimeDB; no dependency on corporate SSO, email, phones or DNS; identity-checked reducers; Secure Shell with short-lived certificates, CA-signed hosts (no trust-on-first-use), Touch ID, two-person approval, read-only forensics, hash-chained recordings |
| 2. Access control, admin can add individuals | People & Access: the admin adds a person with a role via a single-use break-glass enrollment code; admin-only reducers; access events in the audit log |
| 3. Documentation to incident standards, real-time updating and status | The record is structured to NIST SP 800-61, with live phase status, SHA-256 chain of custody and PDF export |
| 4. Scope of compromised data and its status | Data Scope, every asset: intact, accessed, exfil suspected, exfil confirmed, locked by ransomware, restored, evidence preserved |
| 5. Real-time communications | War Room channels (#command, #legal, #exec, #comms-pr, #vendors), Scribe's brief ("what we know / what we don't know yet"), tasks, decision log, shift handoff |

Judging criteria: **security assuming the attacker has every internal system** (we depend on none of them); **ease of use under stress** (one card, one keystroke, a plain-language brief, progressive disclosure); **creativity** (agents contain the machine while the humans coordinate somewhere the attacker can't read).

**NMC²: Keep the World Running.** Their three named failures map one to one. Missed warnings: Sentry fuses six weak signals that no single tool calls an incident. Unclear handoffs: tasks with owners, a decision log and Scribe's shift handoff on one live record. Wrong information at the wrong time: one approval card with evidence, scope and rollback at the moment of decision, plus a plain-language brief for everyone else. And the hall keeps running: one compartment is sealed while eleven neighbors restart on clean hosts. In Uptime Institute's latest survey data, one in five operators said their most recent major outage cost more than $1M ([ITWeb on Uptime 2026](https://itweb.africa/article/uptime-announces-annual-outage-analysis-report-2026/WnxpEv4Y6837V8XL)).

**NVIDIA: Use Nemotron Beyond a Chatbot.** Nobody chats with these agents. Nemotron drives four agents through nine tools (`list_recent_signals`, `open_incident`, `get_host_inventory`, `check_reachability`, `record_finding`, `get_policy`, `propose_action`, `list_events`, `file_report`) against a live database: 15 turns and 14 tool calls in one logged run. Tool integration is real (every effect is a SpacetimeDB reducer call), and so is the engineering around a small model: schema validation, retry on malformed calls, stall detection, completion judged by database state rather than the model's word, and a deterministic fallback with provenance tags. It runs on-prem because incident telemetry is the one dataset you can't send out mid-breach, and the policy gate is what makes a small model safe to act.

**Spacetime: Build on Spacetime.** The majority of the backend isn't a stretch here; it's nearly all of it. All incident state, operator identities and roles, admin-only reducers, the policy gate (auto, needs approval, denied, failing closed), War Room messages, data scope and the documentation live in one SpacetimeDB module on Maincloud, and every console subscribes. The database is the referee: an action the policy refuses never commits. Public repo, booth access code on the submission.

**MLH: Best Domain Name from GoDaddy Registry.** claura.tech is short, brandable and live. Caveat: ICANN lists Radix, not GoDaddy Registry, as the .tech registry ([ICANN](https://www.icann.org/en/registry-agreements/details/tech)), so confirm eligibility with MLH before entering (SUBMISSION.md has the fallback).

