### Weakest line

> “A refused action never commits, so it can't run.”

This is technically confused. If nothing commits, the blocked row, audit event, and synchronized UI state cannot exist. The proposal should commit as blocked; the executable action should not.

**Replacement — FINAL-PITCH.md §7 and DEVPOST “How we built it”:**

> “The reducer commits the proposal as blocked for audit and live synchronization, but creates no executable action.”

